    {
      "id": 901,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [60, 100],
      "size": [560, 900],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 42,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Motion: move a photo along a depth guide on LTX 2.3",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Motion: move a photo along a depth guide on LTX 2.3\n\nRenders the person in your photo moving along your guide video, on LTX 2.3 22B distilled with its union control IC-LoRA. The guide is a depth video you made, such as one rendered in Blender: its frames go straight to the IC-LoRA, with no pose detector, so the guide sets the camera path, the blocking and the timing. Your photo sets the first frame, so the face, the clothes and the light come from your photo. The video starts on the first frame the model makes, after your photo, and has the guide's frame count and frame rate, with no sound. Built from Comfy's template video_ltx2_3_ic_lora, which guides with depth.\n\n## Models\n\n- [ltx-2.3-22b-distilled-fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.3-fp8/resolve/main/ltx-2.3-22b-distilled-fp8.safetensors): LTX 2.3 22B distilled, fp8, with its video and audio VAEs, [LTX-2 Community License](https://github.com/Lightricks/LTX-2/blob/main/LICENSE-2).\n- [ltx-2.3-22b-ic-lora-union-control-ref0.5.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.3-22b-IC-LoRA-Union-Control/resolve/main/ltx-2.3-22b-ic-lora-union-control-ref0.5.safetensors): LTX 2.3 union control IC-LoRA, [LTX-2 Community License](https://github.com/Lightricks/LTX-2/blob/main/LICENSE-2).\n- [gemma_3_12B_it_fp4_mixed.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/ltx-2/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/gemma_3_12B_it_fp4_mixed.safetensors): Gemma 3 12B text encoder, fp4, [Gemma Terms of Use](https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms).\n\nRosesfield ships no weights. Each loader lists its file with a download link.\n\nPart of [Rosesfield](https://github.com/rossaai/rosesfield), MIT. Built from Comfy-Org/workflow_templates, MIT, per NOTICE."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
  ],
